mission "A Bargain with Black Jack"
    name "A Bargain with Black Jack"
    description "Negotiate with a notorious pirate captain who claims to know a safe channel into the western shoals."
    source "Port Azure"
    destination "Gallows Key"
    reward 1655
    speaker offer "Black Jack Rourke"
    speaker visit "Black Jack Rourke"
    speaker complete "Black Jack Rourke"
    to offer
        has "The Fleet at the Blue Line: done"
    on offer
        conversation
            `Black Jack Rourke is waiting in a room above the tavern. The shutters are closed, and the captain has placed a chart between two untouched glasses of rum.`
            `Rourke taps the chart with one finger. "I know a safe channel through the western shoals. I also know what it is worth. Do not look at me like that, captain; a man can be a pirate and still understand arithmetic."`
            choice
                `"You have my attention. What needs doing first?"`
                    accept
                `"Who stands to gain if the truth stays buried?"`
                    goto details
                `"I have no wish to become a pawn in someone else's quarrel."`
                    close
            label details
                `He turns the chart so you can see the soundings. "You want the passage, I want a price, and neither of us needs to pretend this is friendship. Hear my terms before you decide whether the chart is worth the gold."`
                choice
                    `"All right. I will follow the evidence."`
                        accept
                    `"My answer has not changed. I will not sail."`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted A Bargain with Black Jack. Negotiate with a notorious pirate captain who claims to know a safe channel into the western shoals."
    on visit
        conversation
            `At Gallows Key, Rourke shows you the marked channel and checks the depths against his own notes. "There. Safe enough for a careful ship, provided the tide is with you. I make no promises to fools who sail at low water."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Rourke pockets his share with a grin. "A bargain is a bargain. You have the channel, I have my money, and we can both go back to distrusting one another in peace."`
        log "Completed A Bargain with Black Jack. Received 1655 gold. Negotiate with a notorious pirate captain who claims to know a safe channel into the western shoals."
